WEBVTT

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:39.910
How are they doing?

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.290
Sir, the energy readings are increasing,

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.950
but the barrier has not been raised yet.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.750
They can't attack us if we spread our barrier.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.210
Prepare to attack.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.550
Open all turrets.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.880
Load them with guided missiles and aerial depth bombs.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:57.840
Aye, aye!

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.940
Aerial depth bombs ready.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.230
Send power to all turrets.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.820
Target acquisition complete.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.610
Homing device ready.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.200
Every section ready to attack.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.660
Open fire!

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.640
Damn!

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.230
So tenacious!

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.070
Discharge the active laser beam.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:14.540
Homing laser!

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:15.500
Aye!

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.260
Damn them!

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.440
Now, charge Red Noah!

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.900
Aye, aye!

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.660
Damn, the barrier!

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.750
That's right! How long can you withstand

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.040
a barrier of one billion volts?

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.510
Second turret has been taken out.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.170
Third deck is seriously damaged.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.340
Full power to engines! Get us out of this!

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.740
Burn New Nautilus, along with Paris.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.330
The Eiffel Tower!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.300
That won't be all if that ship goes into full-scale action.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.760
That's right, the whole world will be like this.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:47.970
Yes! In order to stop it, we've got to bring it down.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.930
Fools! They think they can bring down the Red Noah.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:54.190
How is he going to do that?

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:59.270
This is bad! It's no use making a frontal attack.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.860
There's a barrier also.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.320
We should destroy it from within on the Gratan.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.700
But how can you get inside?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.080
Open the electromagnetic barrier. Bring the pressure up to maximum.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.200
But our barrier won't last more than a minute!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.920
Forget that! We must charge it at full speed!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.380
Only a barrier can beat a barrier!

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.970
The Nautilus is approaching from the south.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.970
That damned Nemo, is he going to kill himself in despair?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.020
Barrier spread. Pressure at maximum.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.850
All hands, brace for impact!

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.190
Here we go!

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.740
Surrounding atmosphere has turned to plasma!

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.530
Outside temperature now 60,000 degrees!

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.700
Remaining barrier time just under fifty seconds.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.330
How is their barrier?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.660
Still in good shape!

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.080
Damn, what a strong barrier!

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.090
Have they made a hole yet?

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:07.470
Attack at a single point! Get the bow in! That's enough!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.680
Aye, aye!

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.230
No good, it's not working!

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.690
Barrier time under thirty seconds.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.360
Never mind that! Use the over-booster!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:21.860
Aye!

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.160
The engine is going to explode!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.910
Barrier time under fifteen seconds.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.500
We did it!

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.210
Fire!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:48.050
Yahoo!

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.640
The Gratan is in!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.100
Barrier time five seconds!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.220
Get away quickly!

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.010
Aye, aye!

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.690
Whew! That was close.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.280
Were you worried?

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.490
Good luck, Gratan.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.950
Yahoo!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.200
Right, let's go straight ahead!

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.490
But Senorita, it's a dead-end.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:20.330
Oh, hush! This is a short cut.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.870
Get rid of all obstacles!

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:23.080
Okay!

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:37.180
There will be a road behind us when we're done!

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.560
A small object has penetrated N-block!

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.940
Nautilus remains silent.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.730
What should we do?

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:50.570
Raise the Light of Babel to the point of discharge.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.610
Sir?

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:56.870
Discharge the Light of Babel using the servant star Lucifer.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.250
Red Noah is rising!

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:07.130
We'll follow it! Begin ascent!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:08.090
Roger!

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:23.520
The Nautilus is pursuing us!

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:28.020
Fools! They don't know they are drawing closer to Hell!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.200
We've reached escape velocity.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.490
Closing the wings.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:40.620
Wow! Incredible!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.080
We can see stars, but it's daytime!

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.790
Yes, this is outer space.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.130
Outer space?

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.420
Yes, a place where no human being has ever ventured.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.510
But in the 20th century,

00:08:55.800 --> 00:09:03.230
humanity will find a way to make it out here on its own.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.480
We sure will!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.480
The Earth is really round.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:14.400
I wouldn't have thought the Earth would be so blue.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:19.160
How can men keep fighting on such a beautiful place?

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.040
Light of Babel, preparing for discharge!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.910
Power will be sent to the servant star, Lucifer!

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.460
We've picked up the Nautilus!

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:33.300
Twenty seconds to Light of Babel firing axis.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.220
20,000 meters to the Red Noah!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.850
It's within firing range of the main turret. Shall we fire?

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:42.060
No, it's no use.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:46.020
That's right. We should wait for good news from the Gratan.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:49.980
But they're really late. What are they doing?

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.780
Geez, we got lost at such a crucial moment!

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.990
That's why I said we should go as the road goes.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.490
Shut up! Keep quiet!

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:05.960
I can't think with all this noise!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.630
But why don't they attack us?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.960
They don't care about such a tiny tank as ours.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.340
They don't even take us seriously!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:21.760
My dear Nemo, you must regret that you held us in such low regard.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.560
Thirty seconds to discharge.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.520
Compulsory injector, on.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:30.900
What's going on?

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:33.520
Oh, no! The Tower of Babel is charging!

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:34.480
What?

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.160
The Tower of Babel is ready to fire!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:45.080
Fire of my anger, deliver my divine punishment!

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.460
What's that?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.880
The Light of Babel!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.340
But they can't fire on us directly from that position.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.970
Damn! Lucifer!

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.510
Evasive maneuvers!

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.060
No, spread the barrier!

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.850
But the damage hasn't been repaired yet!

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.190
It's doesn't matter! It's better than a direct hit!

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:13.610
It's coming!

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.500
Direct hit to the Nautilus!

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.920
Electromagnetic shock waves approaching.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:38.340
What's that?

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:39.920
They must be energy shock waves!

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.630
What's that?

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.640
It means the Light of Babel hit the Nautilus!

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:45.510
What?

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.270
Damn, they blew it up!

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.730
What are you talking about? We're not sure yet!

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.440
But it's so much energy...

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:03.030
It must have been vaporized.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.570
No, we're not sure yet.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.580
The screen has been repaired.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.120
Unbelievable, they're still alive!

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.210
Yes, the great ship is still there.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:18.340
But how did it survive?

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:21.260
They must have spread the barrier, using their last bit of energy,

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:24.590
but they are out of it now.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.810
It's checkmate! Give them the final blow.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:28.510
Yes, Sir!

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:32.770
What's going on?

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.980
They're going to fire the Tower of Babel again!

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.270
You mean...

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.230
The Nautilus is still alive!

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.150
Damage to starboard side! The barrier is unusable!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.990
Damn! It will be the end of us if we get hit again!

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.870
Can we destroy Lucifer with the main turret?

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:54.210
No, it will take time to cool down the furnace.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.670
You mean we can't do anything?

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.130
Yeah, all we can manage to do now is to maintain our position.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.560
We don't have time now! Understand?

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.060
Gotcha!

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:16.770
Don't shoot till we break it!

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.980
Three minutes until discharge.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.360
Energy charge in progress.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.740
Transfer power to the electronic accelerator!

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.780
Tower of Babel is recharging.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.530
They're going to give us a final blow.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.660
Any report from the Gratan?

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:31.990
Not yet.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.460
Please, Gratan!

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.210
Not yet, Grandis?

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.250
That wall is the last one.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.250
Okay!

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.550
Damn! The battery is out!

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:47.760
What'll we do?

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.220
Don't worry! We've made it this far.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.810
The wall will break if we hit it with something big enough.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:02.270
Let's go!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.660
We made it!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.250
We're going to smash that up, aren't we?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.710
But we can't use the laser beam anymore.

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:23.670
And we don't have much time either.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.210
What should we do?

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.800
Raise the furnace to the critical point.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:33.260
Captain!

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.230
We'll ram the Nautilus into them when it comes to that point.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:37.680
Yes, Sir!

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.610
The Nautilus is approaching us.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:49.860
How useless.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.910
Fifty seconds to discharge.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.830
Release the last safety catch!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.330
Oh, boy!

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.960
You've got to do something, Hanson!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.460
I've got it! That's it!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.420
That infusion tube!

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.340
Thirty seconds to discharge.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.260
You mean we should keep them apart?

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:15.060
That's right.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.180
But how?

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.770
Senorita, we have the stopper right here.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.860
I see!

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.730
Twenty seconds.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:31.950
Now you'll see what a desperate man can really do!

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.080
Ten seconds to discharge.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.160
8, 7...

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.080
6, 5...

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.040
4, 3...

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.040
2, 1...

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:51.300
What's the matter?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.550
The infusion tube isn't connected!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.010
Impossible!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.690
You can't fire now!

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.980
Please hold on a little longer!

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:11.200
Everything's ready.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.910
Right, let's get out of here!

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.360
Gotcha!

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.740
Thanks, Gratan!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:22.410
Goodbye!

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.130
The Tower of Babel has ceased functioning!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.710
The barrier is gone!

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.720
Good! Charge now!

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.220
The Nautilus is charging us!

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.560
It's okay. Beat them to it.

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.640
Red Noah is also charging.

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.560
It looks like this is it.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.480
Oh, no! We'll be crushed!

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:48.940
All weapons have been repaired!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:49.900
Fire!

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:01.620
Go!

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.130
Nautilus has rammed us!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.250
What? What's he going to do?

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:11.960
Let's move in.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.220
We've been boarded by the Nautilus!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:19.810
This can't be!

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.060
Never mind, leave them alone.

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:22.560
Sir?

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:26.060
This Red Noah will be Nemo's graveyard.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.990
We've penetrated the main housing!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.080
Okay, pull the Gratan back in quickly.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.080
Aye, Sir!

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:44.250
First Officer...

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.330
Yes, Sir.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:51.590
Overload the furnace and escape if I don't come back.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:52.500
Captain?

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:56.550
I have something to do here.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.930
You're going to go rescue Nadia, aren't you?

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.510
Forgive me.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:08.690
Captain, it's natural for a father to try to save his daughter.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:11.060
You don't have to apologize.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:13.940
That's right.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.400
But I'm going with you.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:22.120
Me too.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.370
Jean?

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.420
What is this?

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:32.840
Your weapon.

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:34.420
But...

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:38.130
You must defend your life by yourself.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.590
Understand?

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:41.600
Right.

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.350
A smaller ship has been deployed. It's headed this way.

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:52.270
Bring them here.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:52.900
Yes, Sir!

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:59.030
Ask His Majesty and Princess Nadia to come to the throne room.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:00.110
Yes, Sir!

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:03.830
A father and his son meet after thirteen years...

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:43.320
Come out, Gargoyle! I know you're here!

00:19:56.800 --> 00:19:58.590
It's been a long time, Nemo.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:04.050
Or should I say the King of Tartessos, Eleusis La Arwall?

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:08.010
Thirteen years have passed since last we met.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:11.980
Why do you keep wearing that stifling mask,

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:17.400
Prime Minister of Tartessos, Nemesis La Algol?

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.780
What a nice sound from the past.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.530
I've haven't heard that in thirteen years.

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:24.320
We've thrown away those names.

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:27.830
That's true. We can't go back to those days.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.410
Indeed.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.790
By the way, what is the meaning of all this, Gargoyle?

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:36.210
A trial before God.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.460
A trial?

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:43.680
Yes, you will be sentenced for your crime and punished here.

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:48.260
You said before God. Where is this God?

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:52.350
Here. I am God!

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:56.610
How absurd! Where's the defense counsel?

00:20:56.610 --> 00:21:02.780
You don't need it. God judges you in the name of God.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.490
But for now, bring the witnesses here.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:14.750
Miss Grandis! Sanson! Hanson!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:18.080
And now the executors of the judgment.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.260
Nadia!

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:34.890
Nadia?

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:35.770
Impossible!

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:39.230
Damn you! You took her consciousness away!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:42.940
Correct, she no longer needs it.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:47.320
Now, let the trial commence!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:53.120
Eleusis La Arwall, although you were the king of Atlantis,

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:56.080
you tried to coexist with human beings.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:58.420
It's a natural thing to do.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:02.500
I know the ancient Atlanteans created human beings,

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:06.170
but this world is humanity's now.

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:08.390
It's not mine anymore.

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:12.600
You're wrong. This world is ours!

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:17.060
First of all, men are defective. We can't trust them.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:21.310
They wage war endlessly in order to destroy themselves.

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:24.070
There is no future for their race.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:26.820
We must continue controlling them!

00:22:27.400 --> 00:22:29.200
I don't think so.

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:34.410
You believe in such men. That is why you stand accused.

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:39.420
We don't need such a weak Atlantean.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:52.140
Captain!

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:56.810
Gargoyle!

00:23:03.150 --> 00:23:08.240
You do not have the power to kill me.

00:23:10.950 --> 00:23:12.740
Sorry to disappoint you!

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:18.960
Please, Jean...

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:21.750
Shoot Nadia and Neo!

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:22.750
Shoot!

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:33.050
Oh, it's that brave boy again.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:37.890
But can you shoot Nadia?
